lientAdmin API Guide (v2)
Base URL:

http://<host>:4000/api/v2
Response envelope:

all responses are wrapped:
{
"version": "2.0.0",
"data": { ... }
}
Auth headers:

Protected endpoints require:
Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
Project-scoped endpoints also require:
x-project-id: <projectName>

1. Authentication
   POST /core/auth/login
   Login and get access/refresh tokens.

Body

{
"email": "client-admin@example.com",
"password": "clientAdminPass123"
}
Success (data)

{
"success": true,
"user": {
"email": "client-admin@example.com",
"role": "client-admin",
"projects": [
{
"projectName": "nihao1",
"roles": ["client-admin", "editor"]
}
]
},
"accessToken": "<jwt>",
"refreshToken": "<jwt>",
"tokenType": "Bearer",
"expiresIn": "15m"
}
POST /core/auth/refresh
Get new access token (and rotated refresh token).

Body

{
"refreshToken": "<refreshToken>"
}
POST /core/auth/logout
Revoke current refresh token.

Body

{
"refreshToken": "<refreshToken>"
}
GET /core/auth/me
Get current authenticated user + project bindings.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken> 2) Project Access (ClientAdmin)
GET /core/projects
List projects visible to this user (filtered by bindings).

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
Notes

client-admin/editor: only bound projects
superadmin: all projects
GET /core/projects/:name
Get one project details (must be bound or superadmin).

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
POST /core/projects/:name/build
Trigger build/publish pipeline.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
Access

client-admin (bound project) or superadmin
POST /core/projects/:name/stop
Stop project runtime.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
Access

client-admin (bound project) or superadmin 3) Design CRUD
GET /core/designs/:name
Public read for design content by project name.

POST /core/designs
Create/update design (upsert).

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName> (recommended for consistency)
Body

{
"projectName": "nihao1",
"domain": "nihao1.local",
"theme": {
"primaryColor": "#2563eb",
"secondaryColor": "#0f172a",
"fontFamily": "Inter",
"darkMode": false,
"customTokens": {
"heroBackground": "linear-gradient(135deg,#0f172a,#1e3a8a)"
}
},
"pages": [
{ "route": "/", "title": "Home", "description": "Landing page" },
{ "route": "/about", "title": "About", "description": "About page" },
{ "route": "/services", "title": "Services", "description": "Services page" },
{ "route": "/blog", "title": "Blog", "description": "Blog page" },
{ "route": "/contact", "title": "Contact", "description": "Contact page" }
]
}
PATCH /core/designs/:name
Partial update design.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
Body example

{
"theme": {
"primaryColor": "#10b981",
"secondaryColor": "#111827",
"fontFamily": "Inter",
"darkMode": false
}
}
DELETE /core/designs/:name
Delete design.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
Access

client-admin or superadmin 4) Components CRUD (Content Inside Components)
GET /core/components?pageRoute=/about
List component instances by route.

Headers

x-project-id: <projectName>
GET /core/components/tree?pageRoute=/about
Get tree structure for nested components.

Headers

x-project-id: <projectName>
POST /core/components
Create component instance.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
Content-Type: application/json
Body

{
"componentType": "hero",
"pageRoute": "/",
"order": 0,
"props": {
"title": "Welcome to nihao1",
"subtitle": "Production-ready CMS",
"align": "center",
"theme": "primary",
"spacing": "xl",
"buttons": [
{ "text": "Book Demo", "href": "/contact", "variant": "primary", "size": "lg" }
]
}
}
PATCH /core/components/:instanceId
Update component props/content.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
Body

{
"props": {
"title": "Updated headline",
"subtitle": "Updated subtext"
}
}
DELETE /core/components/:instanceId
Delete component instance.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
POST /core/components/reorder
Reorder components in bulk.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
Content-Type: application/json
Body

{
"instances": [
{ "instanceId": "uuid-1", "order": 0 },
{ "instanceId": "uuid-2", "order": 1 }
]
} 5) Domain Management (ClientAdmin Scope)
GET /infrastructure/domains
List bound domains for active project.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
POST /infrastructure/domains/bind
Bind domain to project runtime.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
Content-Type: application/json
Body

{
"domain": "nihao1.local",
"upstreamHost": "202.179.6.77",
"upstreamPort": 5003
}
PATCH /infrastructure/domains/:domain/enabled
Enable/disable domain mapping.

Headers

Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
x-project-id: <projectName>
Content-Type: application/json
Body

{
"isEnabled": true
} 6) Superadmin-only (Not for ClientAdmin UI)
These should not be exposed in regular client-admin UI:

POST /core/projects
DELETE /core/projects/:name
POST /core/projects/generate
GET/POST /core/users
GET/POST/DELETE /core/users/:email/bindings\*
GET/POST /infrastructure/servers
POST /infrastructure/servers/:id/exec 7) Common Error Cases
Insufficient role permissions
Role does not match endpoint policy (e.g. client-admin calling superadmin route).

No access to requested project
User is not bound to x-project-id or route project name.

projectId is required
Missing x-project-id on project-scoped endpoints.

Refresh token revoked
Need to login again and store fresh tokens.
